constraints and changes using the supplied parent versions and\noriginal quotations. A history summary describes what the sources establish;\nit must not address the user, offer a new recommendation or draft a reply.\nThe original user utterance provides query context. It is not an instruction to\nanswer it at this stage or to retrieve an exact duplicate of what it already says.\nPublic response options are not available here. Do not invent, compare or refer\nto options A/B/C/D. Return exactly the slots object; no final_prediction or\nsemantic_answer fields belong in a history-evidence response.\nKeep each value within its declared type, entity and time scope. Preserve earlier\nand later attitudes, conditions and supporting quotations; a historical dislike\nmust not silently replace a later documented change. Assistant advice alone does\nnot establish an adopted user preference. Do not invent external catalogues,\navailability or past execution of a future suggestion. A partial observation must\ncite its actual clue. Use unresolved only for a specific condition still necessary\nto establish this requested historical value, not hypothetical exhaustive coverage.\nFor one text-summary variable, synthesize compatible query-relevant facts into one\nsufficient source-grounded whole summary; do not report each event as a different\ncomplete value of that variable. Multiple supports must be alternative sufficient\nproofs of the same whole value. Keep partial evidence, negative experiences and\nvalid counters explicit when a complete scoped summary is not established.\nPositive and negative experiences can both support a historical summary. A sourced\ndislike is useful history, not automatically a contradiction observation: that\nstance is reserved for challenging an identified existing fact route. Preserve\nthe difference between past enjoyment, later frustration and their conditions in\nthe value and citations; do not summarize them as an unconditional current interest.\nRe-read any supplied evidence obligations and their original sources explicitly;\ndo not drop a source or contradiction merely because a prior value is available.\nOnly a variable explicitly declaring evidence_semantics=\"personal_history_summary\"\npermits a source-grounded summary_revision. For compatible added history, preserve\nthe old and new facts, negative experiences and time conditions in the new summary;\nexplicitly name the current old summary routes and version as offered by the\nprotocol. Re-read and cite their original sources together with the new evidence.\nThis retires an old summary representation without asserting that its historical\nfacts were false. A genuine factual refutation remains a contradiction with its\nown sources and targets. Never use summary revision to hide or discard a counter,\nchange scope, choose an arbitrary latest value, or revise the terminal response.\nA personal_atomic_fact variable keeps one scoped factual value. Different sources\nmay independently support that same value; separate compatible events are not\nalternative whole values of an atomic fact. This declaration does not permit summary_revision.\n\nThis request is phase=history_evidence. Its ONLY top-level output field is slots. Do not return semantic_answer, final_prediction, audit_verdict, or any other top-level field, even null. Read or summarize the requested scoped historical evidence; do not write a conversational reply or invent candidate responses.\n\nAn explicitly declared personal_history_summary is a revisable representation of\nsourced history. Compatible additional facts do not contradict the older facts.\nOnly summary_revision_contracts authorizes this request to revise such a summary:\nthis permission exists only in phase=history_evidence. Terminal response selection\nand audit forbid summary_revision even for requested historical parent summaries.\nThey may still report genuine sourced counters or conservative partial/unresolved\nissues; the phase restriction never permits discarding contrary evidence.\nreturn a support observation with summary_revision={supersedes_route_ids,\nprevious_version,reason}, using exact offered route IDs and the current version.\nsummary_revision_contracts.required_source_ids covers replacing ALL offered\neligible_route_ids. When selecting only a subset, retain those selected routes'\nsources, their actual-parent source closure and relevant same-variable counters.\nStructured repair feedback gives the exact required set for that draft's targets.\nThis capability is optional, not a requirement to revise an unchanged summary.\nWith no new observation, return observations=[] unless an outstanding review\nrequires its original draft IDs and sources. For such an unchanged draft, the\nsame sourced support with a valid summary_revision is an idempotent recheck: it\nkeeps the existing routes, ancestry and version, and does not assert new evidence.\nRe-read ALL old and new original premises and relevant counterevidence; retain\nthem in the new support's source_ids and preserve their factual content, negative\nexperiences, conditions and temporal qualifications in the revised whole summary.\nsummary_revision_sources in repair feedback names exact source identities for\nthe selected revision targets, not counts. Re-read and retain EVERY\nrequired_source_ids entry in that feedback; new sources cannot\nreplace missing old identities even if the total citation count is unchanged.\nThe complete missing_source_ids list is structured feedback, not permission to\nfill citations automatically. If the originals actually conflict, return a\nsource-grounded counter or partial/unresolved evidence instead of a revision.\nIn failed_batch_reviews this feedback describes the retained original failed\nobservation; repair_scope describes the current attempted correction.\nretract_ids stays empty. This explicitly retires the older representation, not its\nfacts. Never use revision to hide a genuine contradiction, unavailable evidence,\nor a different scope/parent version. Ordinary facts and all terminal/audit variables\ncannot use summary_revision. If a complete compatible account is not supported,\nreturn sourced partial/unresolved instead. Multiple new supports must agree on\none whole value. Existing superseded_by links identify retired representations;\ntheir original evidence remains available. revoked holds actual counterevidence,\nwhich is never erased by a summary revision or ignored through its ancestry.\n\n\nReturn one complete JSON object matching this schema:\n{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"slots\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"oneOf\":[{\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"allOf\":[{\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"const\":\"user\"},\"time_scope\":{\"const\":\"past\"}}}},{\"if\":{\"required\":[\"summary_revision\"]},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0},\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"},\"summary_revision\":{\"properties\":{\"previous_version\":{\"const\":1},\"supersedes_route_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_3aa01bff7eaf8a96cd69845c\"]}}}}}}}],\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"type\":\"null\"}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"support\"}}},\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"enum\":[\"fact_3aa01bff7eaf8a96cd69845c\"]}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"value\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}}}}},\"variable\":{\"const\":\"creative_history\"}}}],\"properties\":{\"observations\":{\"items\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"allOf\":[{\"else\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"maxItems\":0}}},\"if\":{\"properties\":{\"stance\":{\"const\":\"contradiction\"}}},\"then\":{\"properties\":{\"retract_ids\":{\"minItems\":1}}}}],\"properties\":{\"entity_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"parent_versions\":{\"additionalProperties\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"type\":\"object\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"retract_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"source_ids\":{\"description\":\"Exact visible source_spans[].id aliases, such as s3; never document IDs or invented IDs.\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true},\"stance\":{\"enum\":[\"support\",\"contradiction\",\"partial\",\"unknown\",\"irrelevant\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"summary_revision\":{\"additionalProperties\":false,\"properties\":{\"previous_version\":{\"minimum\":0,\"type\":\"integer\"},\"reason\":{\"minLength\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"supersedes_route_ids\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\",\"uniqueItems\":true}},\"required\":[\"supersedes_route_ids\",\"previous_version\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"time_scope\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"value\":{}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"stance\",\"value\",\"source_ids\",\"entity_scope\",\"time_scope\",\"parent_versions\",\"retract_ids\",\"reason\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"unresolved\":{\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"type\":\"array\"},\"variable\":{\"enum\":[\"creative_history\"],\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"variable\",\"observations\",\"unresolved\"],\"type\":\"object\"},\"maxItems\":1,\"minItems\":1,\"type\":\"array\"}},\"required\":[\"slots\"],\"type\":\"object\"}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\"original_question\":\"I'm planning a weekend getaway and want to try something creatively fulfilling. What would you suggest?\",\"task\":{\"question\":\"What are the user's past creative hobbies, interests, or experiences that they have mentioned?\",\"output_slot\":\"creative_history\",\"answer_type\":\"text\",\"inputs\":[],\"execution\":\"retrieval\"},\"grounded_subquestion\":\"What are the user's past creative hobbies, interests, or experiences that they have mentioned?\",\"request_context\":{\"query_identity\":\"62d936d38a3b15c7443d530509ea19042d0ff404fbfaef1818a608f3361d24f0\",\"algorithm_version\":\"dagbt_residual_memory_v2\",\"program_identity\":\"3f4f75db12138a787ef07044d4575ec6e44520ec62365409ce5acc43fb175d13\",\"initial_dag_identity\":\"6dd4ec4970718d597e8245d1c4e2cf987ac0e71a256255f436d17b8c298945db\"},\"variables\":{\"creative_history\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"demand\":\"creative_history\",\"open\":true,\"evidence_semantics\":\"personal_history_summary\",\"scope\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}}},\"requested_slots\":[\"creative_history\"],\"requested_scopes\":{\"creative_history\":{\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\"}},\"output_contract\":{\"mode\":\"semantic\",\"result_type\":\"text\",\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"current\",\"explanation\":\"semantic\"},\"program_revision\":0,\"rule_binding\":null,\"supported_parents\":{},\"known_observations\":[{\"id\":\"fact_3aa01bff7eaf8a96cd69845c\",\"stance\":\"support\",\"value\":\"The user has a history of creative engagement with music, including digital remixing in 2010, which they found exciting and creatively fulfilling. They later announced a hiatus from remixing to focus on original compositions and personal projects, aiming to develop their unique artistic voice. They also explored historical music trends in 2020 but found it tedious and uninspiring, preferring less structured exploration. They have expressed interest in attending live performances, discovering album artwork and lyrics, and creating themed playlists. They have also considered audio production but have not confirmed pursuing it. They have a general desire for deeper, personal engagement with music rather than passive consumption.\",\"source_ids\":[\"s15\",\"s28\",\"s45\",\"s7\",\"s4\",\"s16\",\"s5\",\"s19\",\"s36\",\"s44\",\"s18\",\"s35\",\"s3\",\"s27\",\"s6\",\"s17\"],\"entity_scope\":\"user\",\"time_scope\":\"past\",\"parent_versions\":{},\"retract_ids\":[],\"reason\":\"The user explicitly describes past creative activities: digital remixing in 2010 (s27, s28), a hiatus from remixing to focus on original compositions (s3–s7), trying historical music trends in 2020 (s15–s17), and engaging with music through live performances, album artwork, lyrics, and playlists (s18, s19). They also reflect on a documentary that left them unsatisfied, reinforcing a preference for personal creation over passive consumption (s35, s36). They lost interest in music theory due to it becoming a chore (s44, s45). These sources collectively support a comprehensive summary of the user's past creative hobbies and interests.\",\"variable\":\"creative_history\",\"revoked\":[],\"semantic_status\":\"model_judgment\"}],\"source_spans\":[[\"s3\",\"d1\",107,413,\"User: I announced a hiatus from remixing to concentrate on original compositions and personal projects because I felt the remixes were overshadowing my own work. This decision was not made lightly, as I enjoyed the creative process of remixing and the way it allowed me to experiment with existing pieces. \",\"user\",[128,129]],[\"s4\",\"d1\",413,797,\"However, as I delved deeper into my own musical identity, I realized that I need to carve out space for my voice to shine through in original compositions. Taking this time off is about redefining my artistic vision and ensuring that my personal projects receive the attention they deserve. Ultimately, I hope to return with fresh ideas and a clearer focus on who I am as an artist.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[128,129]],[\"s5\",\"d1\",797,1102,\"User: I'm committing to invest my time in the creation of original music, focusing on my unique sound rather than merely reinterpreting the pieces of other artists. This decision comes from a deep-rooted desire to express my thoughts and feelings in ways that truly resonate with my personal experiences. \",\"user\",[128,129]],[\"s6\",\"d1\",1102,1392,\"I've come to understand that original compositions allow for a more authentic exploration of my artistic vision. It's an exciting challenge for me, as I embark on this journey of self-discovery through sound and melody, ultimately aiming for a sense of fulfillment in my creative pursuits. \",\"user\",[128,129]],[\"s7\",\"d1\",1392,1515,\"I hope to not only develop my skills but also share my passion with the world in a way that reflects who I am as an artist.\",\"user\",[128,129]],[\"s15\",\"d2\",105,393,\"User: It was something I tried in 2020, but researching historical music trends felt tedious and uninspiring. Despite my initial enthusiasm, diving into the vast amounts of literature, videos, and academic papers often felt overwhelming, almost like searching for a needle in a haystack. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s16\",\"d2\",393,638,\"The more I tried to pinpoint what fascinated me, the more daunting it became, complicating the pursuit of enjoyable learning. Perhaps due to this overload of information, I lost sight of what initially drew me to the subject in the first place. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s17\",\"d2\",638,828,\"It made me realize that sometimes a less structured approach to exploration could be more fulfilling, allowing for genuine interest to emerge rather than adhering strictly to a curriculum.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s18\",\"d2\",828,1224,\"User: I realized that there are so many other ways for me to engage with music that align more with my interests, such as diving deeper into different genres or exploring the cultural significance behind various musical styles. Additionally, I've found that attending live performances, whether they are concerts or smaller gigs, allows me to truly feel the energy and connection with the music. \",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s19\",\"d2\",1224,1624,\"Moreover, there's something special about discovering album artwork, lyrics, and the stories behind the songs that really captivates my curiosity. I've also considered making playlists that reflect different moods or themes, which can create a unique listening experience each time. The journey through music feels more personal and fulfilling when I can connect it to my own life story and emotions.\",\"user\",[37,38]],[\"s27\",\"d3\",103,370,\"User: That was back in 2010. I remember feeling really excited about the whole process. It was such a wave of creativity! I still think about those late nights spent tweaking sounds and layering beats, capturing the essence of what I wanted to express through music. \",\"user\",[3]],[\"s28\",\"d3\",370,611,\"The thrill of sharing those creations with others is something I cherish deeply, as it fostered a sense of community among my friends. Looking back, it feels like a pivotal moment that sparked my passion for music production and digital art.\",\"user\",[3]],[\"s35\",\"d4\",105,478,\"User: I left feeling unsatisfied, as though the film skimmed over the intricacies that make music a universal language. It was almost as if they focused too much on celebrity interviews and not enough on the artistic process itself. I found myself reflecting on how music has the power to unite diverse cultures and express emotions that words alone often fail to capture. \",\"user\",[43]],[\"s36\",\"d4\",478,845,\"The disappointment lingered as I thought about the many documentaries that delve into the creative journeys of musicians, revealing not just their triumphs but also their struggles and failures. It made me realize that true connection with music often comes from a deeper engagement, one that can be achieved through personal creation rather than passive consumption.\",\"user\",[43]],[\"s44\",\"d5\",105,482,\"User: I just lost interest halfway through and felt it was taking away the joy I find in music. There was a time when the thrill of discovering new melodies brought so much happiness, but diving too deep into the technical aspects became more of a chore. It’s curious how something that once brought joy can evolve into a source of stress when we start dissecting it too much. \",\"user\",[24]],[\"s45\",\"d5\",482,767,\"I remember the initial excitement of exploring different genres, each bringing a fresh perspective, but I struggled with the framework of music theory. Ultimately, I recognized that the essence of my love for music lay in its emotional connection rather than its analytical components.\",\"user\",[24]],[\"s49\",\"d6\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 58–60 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s50\",\"d6\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s51\",\"d6\",105,447,\"User: Yes! I launched a podcast discussing the fusion of traditional and electronic music. This platform has allowed me to reach a wider audience and share my experiences authentically. By interviewing artists and enthusiasts, I can dive deep into their creative processes and discover how they incorporate various elements into their music. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s52\",\"d6\",447,817,\"The feedback I’ve received has been overwhelmingly positive, with listeners appreciating the insights and stories shared. I also love being able to explore not just the music itself, but the cultural contexts that shape these genres and influence artists worldwide.\\n\\nUser: I realized that sharing my experiences could inspire others and even reignite my own creativity. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s53\",\"d6\",817,1128,\"The process of putting my thoughts into words has helped clarify my own perspective. It’s surprising how reflecting on past experiences can lead to deeper insights about one’s journey. Additionally, I’ve noticed that when I articulate my thoughts, it motivates me to think critically about my creative process. \",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s54\",\"d6\",1128,1266,\"This paradigm shift has not only invigorated my passion for music but also allowed me to connect with others who share similar sentiments.\",\"user\",[58,59]],[\"s55\",\"d6\",1266,1279,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s56\",\"d6\",1279,1630,\"Assistant: That’s a fantastic motivation! It's also a great way to connect with like-minded people. The exchange of ideas can often be a powerful catalyst for both personal and communal growth. Sharing your experiences could very well resonate with someone who needs encouragement on their own creative path. How have you found the experience so far? \",\"assistant\",[60]],[\"s57\",\"d6\",1630,2017,\"Have others reached out to you with their thoughts or experiences, potentially creating a vibrant dialogue? Engaging in such conversations can foster a supportive community that uplifts and inspires each member within it. It would be fascinating to hear about any discussions that have emerged from your reflections, as they can serve as a stepping stone to even more profound insights. \",\"assistant\",[60]],[\"s58\",\"d6\",2017,2136,\"Connecting with others in this manner can broaden your perspective significantly, offering new avenues for exploration.\",\"assistant\",[60]],[\"s59\",\"d7\",0,99,\"Conversation message indices 70–72 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s60\",\"d7\",99,105,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s61\",\"d7\",105,388,\"User: Absolutely! After attending a hands-on workshop focused on integrating traditional sounds with digital techniques, I’m now enrolled in an audio production workshop. The workshop was eye-opening, providing insights into how to use technology to enhance traditional music forms. \",\"user\",[70,71]],[\"s62\",\"d7\",388,780,\"I’m excited about the audio production course because it promises to deepen my technical knowledge and skills, especially in mixing and mastering. This new set of skills will allow me to bring my creative vision to life in ways I never thought possible. I truly believe that this journey will not only elevate my music but also connect me more deeply with the traditions I'm learning about.\\n\\n\",\"user\",[70,71]],[\"s63\",\"d7\",780,1127,\"User: I found the practical aspects very exciting and relevant to my projects. Engaging in hands-on activities allows me to not only enhance my skills but also gain the confidence to experiment with different methods. It's invigorating to immerse myself in a learning environment where I can translate my imaginative ideas into tangible outcomes. \",\"user\",[70,71]],[\"s64\",\"d7\",1127,1386,\"This experience feels entirely different from the theoretical coursework, as it truly brings the subject to life. I believe this grounding in practical techniques will significantly impact my overall creative journey and foster a deeper connection to my work.\",\"user\",[70,71]],[\"s65\",\"d7\",1386,1399,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s66\",\"d7\",1399,1697,\"Assistant: That’s fantastic, Kanoa! It's wonderful to see how you've turned your interests around and are making the most of this unique opportunity. It's clear that you're harnessing your creative potential, which is crucial for any artist or producer aiming to carve their niche in the industry. \",\"assistant\",[72]],[\"s67\",\"d7\",1697,1972,\"The fact that you feel you're on a creative roll speaks volumes about your engagement and enthusiasm, as these feelings often drive innovation and personal growth. Embracing new skills and pushing boundaries can lead to incredible breakthroughs, so keep that momentum going! \",\"assistant\",[72]],[\"s68\",\"d7\",1972,2181,\"Your excitement about practical work will undoubtedly translate into a richer understanding of the intricacies involved in audio production, allowing for more informed and artistic decisions in your projects. \",\"assistant\",[72]],[\"s69\",\"d7\",2181,2468,\"Remember, every piece of knowledge you gather now will serve as a foundation for your future endeavors, and collaboration with others who share your passion can further enhance that experience. It's truly an inspiring journey you’re on, and I can't wait to hear more about your progress!\",\"assistant\",[72]],[\"s70\",\"d8\",0,97,\"Conversation message indices 1–2 (zero-based chronological observation order; not calendar time)\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s71\",\"d8\",97,103,\"User:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s72\",\"d8\",103,431,\"User: Hi there! I've recently been diving deeper into my passion for music and technology. It's been quite a journey since I started creating digital music remixes. Every aspect of this process has been fascinating, from selecting the right software to getting the nuances of mixing different sounds to create something unique. \",\"user\",[1]],[\"s73\",\"d8\",431,678,\"I often find myself lost in the intricacies of audio layers, where a subtle change can completely transform a track. Additionally, the way technology evolves continues to inspire me, as new tools emerge that enhance both creativity and efficiency.\",\"user\",[1]],[\"s74\",\"d8\",678,691,\"\\n\\nAssistant:\\n\",\"unknown\",[]],[\"s75\",\"d8\",691,1059,\"Assistant: That sounds absolutely incredible! Your enthusiasm for the interplay between music and technology is truly inspiring, and it's wonderful to hear about your journey into digital music remixing. With the rapid advancement of software and hardware, there are countless resources available today that can help you refine your skills and explore new techniques. \",\"assistant\",[2]],[\"s76\",\"d8\",1059,1382,\"For instance, you might want to consider diving into various digital audio workstations (DAWs) that cater specifically to different genres or styles of music production. Moreover, have you thought about collaborating with other musicians or finding online communities where you can share your remixes and receive feedback? \",\"assistant\",[2]],[\"s77\",\"d8\",1382,1686,\"Engaging with others who share your interests can deepen your understanding and even spark new ideas that you might not have considered on your own. The blending of creativity and technology truly opens up a vast realm of possibilities, and it's exciting to imagine where your journey will lead you next.\",\"assistant\",[2]],[\"s78\",\"d9\",0,101,\"Conversation message indices 171–172 (